# The other way round: Ritual Chamber cast first (a Demon as it enters, CR 709.5h), then Unholy Annex's door unlocked on
# turn 3 for its {2}{B} (CR 709.5e). The Room goes from Ritual Chamber alone, mana value 5, to both names and 8. Unlocking
# the left door triggers nothing - "when you unlock this door" is Ritual Chamber's, and the Room still has the one Demon -
# but gives the Room Annex's end step ability, which with a Demon to count draws a card, drains the opponent for 2 and gains
# Bot1 2 life. Black Lotus, Mox Jet and a Swamp pay for the first cast; the Jet and two Swamps for the unlock.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Black Lotus
Unholy Annex // Ritual Chamber
Mox Jet
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Unholy Annex // Ritual Chamber.Cast(Ability: Ritual Chamber)
Bot1.Pass
[T1 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ritual Chamber.Doors = Ritual Chamber
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ritual Chamber.ManaValue = 5
? Bot1.Battlefield.Demon Token.Power = 6
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Ritual Chamber.Activate(Ability: left door)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp#2.Activate
? Stack.Count = 0
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Unholy Annex // Ritual Chamber.Doors = Unholy Annex; Ritual Chamber
? Bot1.Battlefield.Unholy Annex // Ritual Chamber.ManaValue = 8
[T4 Bot2.Upkeep]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Demon Token; Mox Jet; Swamp; Swamp; Unholy Annex // Ritual Chamber
Bot1.Life = 22
Bot2.Life = 18
